  "content": {
    "id": "p56-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "When a polynomial is divided by $(2x+1)(x-3)$, the remainder is $3x-1$.\nWhat is the remainder when the polynomial is divided by $2x+1$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-\\frac{5}{2}$, since $P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)=3\\left(-\\frac12\\right)-1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(2x+1)(x-3)Q(x)+(3x-1)\\\\P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)&=\\left(2\\left(-\\frac12\\right)+1\\right)\\left(-\\frac12-3\\right)Q\\left(-\\frac12\\right)+3\\left(-\\frac12\\right)-1\\\\P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)&=-\\frac32-1\\\\P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)&=-\\frac52\\end{align*}$$\nBy the remainder theorem, the remainder is $-\\frac52$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
